Use a nested write: call `guild.update` and put the `PremiumModel` changes inside the `premium` relation field. Adapted to your schema (the docs show the same pattern with `post.update` → `author`):

```ts
await prisma.guild.update({
  where: { guildId: "123" },
  data: {
    premium: {
      upsert: {                       // update if it exists, else create
        create: { active: true, subtype_monthly: true },
        update: { active: true, subtype_monthly: true },
      },
    },
  },
  include: { premium: true },
});
```

If the premium row already exists, use `premium: { update: { active: false } }` instead. The reference's one-to-one form also allows `update: { where: {...}, data: {...} }`.

Sources:
- `apps/docs/content/docs/orm/v7/prisma-client/queries/relation-queries.mdx`, "Nested writes → Update or create a related record" (lines 1016–1047).
- `apps/docs/content/docs/orm/v7/reference/prisma-client-reference.mdx`, "One-to-one relations → Nested update example" (lines 5206–5217).

I adapted the examples to your models. The docs don't use `Guild`/`PremiumModel`, and I haven't run this against your schema.

